      "id": "n1",
      "kind": "grammar",
      "title": "मुझे … चाहिए",
      "text": "Hindi does not say \"I want tea\". It says, word for word, \"to me, tea is needed\": मुझे चाय चाहिए. For someone else the person gets को: रवि को चाय चाहिए.",
      "explains": [
        "hi.chahiye",
        "hi.postposition-ko"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "n2",
      "kind": "usage",
      "title": "आप",
      "text": "आप is the respectful \"you\", used with adults you do not know well. It takes the same verb as \"they\": आपको, आप कैसे हैं.",
      "explains": [
        "hi.hum-aap-main"
      ],
      "afterScenes": 1
    }
  ],
